{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Common Issues When Data Migrating"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about issues in data migration."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Implement data migration processes and data backups within the IT solution.  Understand the different types of data movements, making an emphasis on data migration movements as well as data backups."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on software testing, test estimation, and data migration processes"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adjectives Ending in \u2013Ed and \u2013Ing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are two different types of <b>adjectives</b>, the ones that end in <b>\u2013ed</b> and the ones that end in <b>\u2013ing</b>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A suffix is a particle that we add at the end of a word. In this case, the suffix <b>\u2013ed</b> and <b>\u2013ing</b> help us create different adjectives with different meanings. </br></br>The <b>adjectives that end in \u2013ed</b> help us describe emotions; in simple words, they describe the way someone feels about something. </br></br>For example:</br><i>I was very <b>bored</b> in the technology class.</br>  She was <b>surprised</b> by the way data migrates. </br> I feel <b>confused</b> about what migration technology I should use."}, {"type": "text", "content": "On the other hand, the <b>adjectives that end in \u2013ing</b> describe a situation. </br></br>For example:</br><i>The technology class was very <b>boring</b>. </br> The way data migrates is <b>surprising</b>! </br>Data migration can seem <b>stressing</b> at first, but you just need to practice."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm reading an interesting article that might help us with our presentation next week."}, {"type": "example", "content": "However, data migration is something necessary and once it's achieved, it's really satisfying."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Even though the migration process makes you feel exhausted, it is also fulfilling to know everything works well after such effort. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Types of Data Migration"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are different types of <b>data migration</b> people can use to migrate files according to the different features a project has."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We can subdivide data migration in two categories: <b>Array-to-array</b> and <b>file-to-file</b>. Additionally, the <span class=\"strong\"> array-to-array</span> can be divided into the following types:  <br /><br /><ul> <li>\t<span class=\"strong\"> Host based</span>: Copying volumes at host level. <li><span class=\"strong\"> Array based</span>: Moving data between arrays.  <li><span class=\"strong\"> Hypervisor based</span>: To move virtual machines between storage on varied arrays.  <li><span class=\"strong\"> Virtualization appliance based</span>: To abstract the storage from the host using an app. It allows seamless migration. <li><span class=\"strong\"> Virtual array based</span>: Virtualizing external storage and moving data between arrays <br /><br />The other type is the <span class=\"strong\"> file-to-file </span>modality, which is equally complex in order to make data available to users during and after the migration process, and not affecting the location or address of such files."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "outage "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an intentional and temporary suspension of activities or operation  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Operational dependencies represent a huge issue because IT departments work 24/7, which makes it difficult to meet the conditions to migrate data without outage."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dependency "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the feeling of reliance on something or somebody"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Technical dependencies make such projects run slow and increase the cost because some software and hardware need to be updated before the data migration."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "daunting "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "discouraging  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Wow, data migration might be discouraging and daunting."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sum up "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to synthetize or condense the most relevant aspects of a topic"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To sum up, there are host based, array based, hypervisor based, virtualization appliance based, and virtual array based."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "virtualization "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a simulation done in a computer   "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To sum up, there are host based, array based, hypervisor based, virtualization appliance based, and virtual array based."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "seamless "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "with no interruption   "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The last ones allow seamless data migration."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you work for a company that needs to make a data migration process."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a plan to make the data migration. Be specific, tell which type of process you would use and why."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a document with your plan."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present the plan to a partner and ask his/her question about it."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I create a plan for a data migration process"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a document explaining my plan."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my plan to a partner and answer questions about it. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about common issues that can cause problems in the data migration process."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe array-to-array data migrations."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain the file-to-file data migrations process."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are the most significant advantages of data migration?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content